A cube is painted on exactly four faces exactly when it is glued to exactly **two** other cubes.

Read the shape: a column of 4 cubes on the left; a front row of 3 more cubes to its right; behind the right-most front cube one more cube, and behind that a back row of 3 cubes (the right-most one carrying one cube on top).

Go along the shape:
- the top cube of the left column touches 1 cube; the other three cubes of the column touch 2;
- the 3 front-row cubes and the cube behind the right one touch 2 each;
- the right cube of the back row touches 3 (the cube in front of it, the cube on top, its left neighbour);
- the cube on top touches 1; the middle back cube touches 2; the left back cube touches 1.

Cubes touching exactly 2 others: $3+4+1 = 8$.

**Answer: (C) 8**
